               "Relate a rectangle's area to rows of unit squares.\nCalculate rectangular area using length times width.",
               "Area measures a surface. In a rectangle, the number of unit squares in each row times the number of rows gives A = length x width. Convert length and width to the same unit before multiplying.\n\nWorked example: A classroom floor is 8 m by 6 m. Its area is 8 x 6 = 48 m^2. For a card 20 cm by 0.3 m, convert 0.3 m to 30 cm, so area = 20 x 30 = 600 cm^2. Multiplying a measurement in cm directly by one in m does not produce cm^2.",
               "Draw a 6 cm by 4 cm rectangle on centimetre grid paper and count its squares. Compare with multiplication. Measure a desk top and calculate its area.",
